Description: Rapid light curves obtained via the pulse-amplitude modulation (PAM) technique are widely used to characterize photosynthesis, but extracting kinetic parameters requires fitting regression models to raw data. The pam R package automates this process, enabling fast, reproducible analysis using established models (Vollenweider 1965; Platt et al. 1980; Eilers & Peeters 1988; Walsby 1997).
